From: CoolFreeze23 <34906576+CoolFreeze23@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: drop partial MSDUs on the WBM error path

ath12k_dp_rx_h_undecap_raw() WARNs on a RAW-decap MSDU that is not both
first and last and then returns without trimming it, so the caller
delivers the frame to mac80211 with FCS and crypto trailer attached.
Both WBM-error callers can get there:

- the RXDMA error handlers (unauth-WDS, TKIP MIC) parse every buffer as
  a complete MSDU with its own rx descriptor, but only the first buffer
  of a scattered MSDU has one; the others are parsed from payload bytes.
  Drop scattered MSDUs released by RXDMA as a whole.
- the null-queue-descriptor and TKIP-MIC paths do not filter RAW MSDUs
  that are not first+last. Drop them before undecap.

Also log a TQM completion for an already-unmapped peer at debug level,
as the HTT completion path already does. It is expected when a station
leaves with frames in flight (issue #86's "failed to find the peer with
peer_id" bursts).
---
diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wifi7/dp_rx.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wifi7/dp_rx.c
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wifi7/dp_rx.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wifi7/dp_rx.c
@@ -1624,6 +1624,10 @@ static int ath12k_wifi7_dp_rx_h_null_q_desc(struct ath12k_pdev_dp *dp_pdev,
 	if (rxcb->is_continuation)
 		return -EINVAL;
 
+	if (rx_info->decap_type == DP_RX_DECAP_TYPE_RAW &&
+	    !(rxcb->is_first_msdu && rxcb->is_last_msdu))
+		return -EINVAL;
+
 	if (!rx_info->msdu_done) {
 		ath12k_warn(ab,
 			    "msdu_done bit not set in null_q_des processing\n");
@@ -1681,6 +1685,11 @@ static bool ath12k_wifi7_dp_rx_h_tkip_mic_err(struct ath12k_pdev_dp *dp_pdev,
 	rxcb->is_first_msdu = rx_info->is_first_msdu;
 	rxcb->is_last_msdu = rx_info->is_last_msdu;
 
+	if (rxcb->is_continuation ||
+	    (rx_info->decap_type == DP_RX_DECAP_TYPE_RAW &&
+	     !(rxcb->is_first_msdu && rxcb->is_last_msdu)))
+		return true;
+
 	if ((hal_rx_desc_sz + l3pad_bytes + msdu_len) > DP_RX_BUFFER_SIZE) {
 		ath12k_dbg(ab, ATH12K_DBG_DATA,
 			   "invalid msdu len in tkip mic err %u\n", msdu_len);
@@ -2016,6 +2025,18 @@ int ath12k_wifi7_dp_rx_process_wbm_err(struct ath12k_dp *dp,
 			continue;
 		}
 
+		if (!skb_queue_empty(&scatter_msdu_list) &&
+		    err_info.err_rel_src == HAL_WBM_REL_SRC_MODULE_RXDMA) {
+			/* The RXDMA error handlers parse each buffer as a
+			 * complete MSDU with its own rx descriptor, but only
+			 * the first buffer of a scattered MSDU carries one.
+			 * Drop the whole scattered MSDU.
+			 */
+			ath12k_dp_clean_up_skb_list(&scatter_msdu_list);
+			dev_kfree_skb_any(msdu);
+			continue;
+		}
+
 		if (!skb_queue_empty(&scatter_msdu_list)) {
 			struct sk_buff *msdu;
 
diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wifi7/dp_tx.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wifi7/dp_tx.c
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wifi7/dp_tx.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wifi7/dp_tx.c
@@ -859,7 +859,8 @@ static void ath12k_wifi7_dp_tx_complete_msdu(struct ath12k_pdev_dp *dp_pdev,
 
 	peer = ath12k_dp_link_peer_find_by_peerid(dp_pdev, ts->peer_id);
 	if (!peer || !peer->sta) {
-		ath12k_err(ab,
+		/* expected for frames completing after the peer was deleted */
+		ath12k_dbg(ab, ATH12K_DBG_DP_TX,
 			   "dp_tx: failed to find the peer with peer_id %d\n",
 			   ts->peer_id);
 		ieee80211_free_txskb(ath12k_pdev_dp_to_hw(dp_pdev), msdu);
